leAnnual","model":null,"zone":"windowDressing","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T05:50:40.831Z","evidenceHash":"14b008dc13e61b3fa9849d0c8d168c8441c4cfe5301e39258ae29d2ea76163e0"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/KTOS.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/KTOS.png","website":"https://www.kratosdefense.com","ceo":"Eric DeMarco","full_time_employees":"4300","description":"Kratos Defense & Security Solutions, Inc. primarily functions as a contractor for the United States Department of Defense. Its business operations are organized into two distinct divisions: Kratos Government Solutions and Unmanned Systems. The Kratos Government Solutions segment delivers a comprehensive suite of products and services, including advanced microwave electronics, solutions for space and satellite communications, specialized training and cybersecurity/warfare capabilities, C5ISR (Command, Control, Communications, Computers, Combat Systems, Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance) and modular systems, cutting-edge turbine technologies, and essential defense and rocket support services. Meanwhile, the Unmanned Systems division is dedicated to developing and supplying autonomous platforms, specifically unmanned aerial, ground, and maritime systems. Kratos caters to an extensive client base, which includes various national security organizations, the DoD, intelligence and classified agencies, international government bodies, and both domestic and global commercial enterprises. The company was established in 1994 and its corporate headquarters are located in San Diego, California.","description_en":"Kratos Defense & Security Solutions, Inc. primarily functions as a contractor for the United States Department of Defense. Its business operations are organized into two distinct divisions: Kratos Government Solutions and Unmanned Systems. The Kratos Governme